   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many runners start too fast and fade. A coach teaches a negative split, running the second half faster, and her runners improved, though hills and heat can upset the plan.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coach Achterberg is the best coach in the region, and every runner should copy her plan if they want to win.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Runners check their watches at each half-mile marker and learn what an even effort feels like over several weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Runners who start fast always lose, so the coach forbids her team from passing anyone until the final mile.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many runners start too fast and fade. A coach teaches a negative split, running the second half faster, and her runners improved, though hills and heat can upset the plan.$q$, $q$The third choice covers the problem, the plan, the results and the limits without adding judgments. The first choice gives opinions, such as "best coach," that the passage never states.$q$, 'draft', 'f8986b94-c83e-5075-9917-4d2b7cdc8c2d')
