   $q$Keisha calls standby for Bao "in a voice so calm that he almost forgot two hundred people were watching." What can be inferred about Keisha from this detail?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is still too dizzy to speak in a normal voice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She wants Bao to feel the pressure she felt in act one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She puts aside her own disappointment to help Bao succeed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is relieved that she never has to run the board again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She puts aside her own disappointment to help Bao succeed.$q$, $q$After losing her job for the night, Keisha still steadies Bao with a calm voice, which shows she is supporting him. The calm voice helps him forget the pressure, so it does the opposite of making him feel it.$q$, 'draft', '35c073ad-d385-59ff-94db-6d992a259a4d')
