insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9e5581a7-cc51-55cf-bbfe-3a865c3b4e22', 'rg9-text-structure-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-text-structure'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Piano for the Station$q$, $q$The waiting room of the Harwell train station is one of the busiest spaces in our town, and also one of the dullest. Hundreds of people pass through it every day, staring at their phones or at the departure board. I believe the town should place a public piano in that room, free for anyone to play.

First, a piano would give the space a sense of life. In the nearby city of Dunmore, a piano placed in the bus terminal three years ago is rarely silent. Commuters stop to play a few bars before work, and children pick out simple tunes while their parents buy tickets. A terminal survey found that most travelers said the music made their wait more pleasant.

Second, a public piano gives people a chance to share a skill they rarely get to show. Many adults took lessons as children but no longer own an instrument. A piano in a public place invites them to play again, and it lets young musicians perform for a real audience without the pressure of a formal recital.

Some residents worry that the piano would be damaged or that the noise would bother travelers. These are fair concerns, but Dunmore has answered them. Its piano is covered with a locked lid at night, and a volunteer tunes and checks it once a month. Travelers who want quiet can use the smaller waiting area upstairs.

A used piano costs less than a single new bench for the platform. The town council meets on the first Tuesday of next month, and I urge every resident who agrees to attend and speak in favor of the idea. Our station could become a place people remember, not just a place they pass through.$q$, 'draft')
