values
  ('660e4a51-1067-524e-afaa-3d7f3272f741', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final scene develop the theme beyond what Tomas discovers at home?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Tomas wants revenge and plans to keep challenging Lin until he finally wins.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It shows his change lasting, since he now treats a loss as a chance to learn alongside the player who beat him.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that studying the notebook finally allows Tomas to defeat Lin in their rematch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It suggests that Mrs. Adeyemi is disappointed that Tomas still cannot beat a younger player.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows his change lasting, since he now treats a loss as a chance to learn alongside the player who beat him.$q$, $q$Tomas loses again but stays behind "arguing happily" with Lin over the notebook, so his new attitude toward losing continues. The text says he lost the rematch, so the choice about defeating Lin contradicts it.$q$, 'draft', 'c542e562-63e4-56f5-9fec-55eb5210faad')
