values
  ('2c9e8e60-b9b0-5d55-8406-2e97aecbd593', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final stanza develop the theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It applies the butterflies' pattern to the speaker's own life, turning a scene from nature into a lesson about human effort.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It moves to a new subject that is unrelated to the butterflies in earlier stanzas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-connection"},{"text":"It reveals that the speaker once watched the butterflies leave the mountain firs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the speaker regrets planting trees that will take years to grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It applies the butterflies' pattern to the speaker's own life, turning a scene from nature into a lesson about human effort.$q$, $q$The speaker thinks of the migration when starting work, like planting a tree, that others will finish, which connects the image back to people. The return to "orange coming loose in March" shows the stanza is linked to the butterflies, not unrelated.$q$, 'draft', 'cb146cb0-3216-53e1-887d-2b0f5e020adb')
