  ('eb55b13c-8ae2-5c20-9585-ca18d4715a9c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Working before sunrise is lonely and makes people unhappy with their jobs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Baking bread requires waking up early and folding dough with care.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Quiet work that no one notices can still hold a community's daily life together.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Customers should always thank the baker by name when they buy bread.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Quiet work that no one notices can still hold a community's daily life together.$q$, $q$The father's unseen work means "The town is fed" and the morning "starts the way it should." The speaker decides "he likes it so," which contradicts the idea that his work makes him unhappy.$q$, 'draft', 'e1083313-f281-5516-b4ab-a092af8eabbf')
