   $q$The Latin root migr means "to move from place to place." What are "migratory birds"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Birds that travel between different regions each year","is_correct":true},{"text":"Birds that build their nests on top of tall buildings","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Birds that stay in one city park for their whole lives","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Birds that sing loud calls to warn of hunting hawks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Birds that travel between different regions each year$q$, $q$Migr means "to move," and the passage says the birds "travel thousands of kilometers between their winter homes and their summer nesting grounds." Staying in one park is the opposite of moving from place to place.$q$, 'draft', '1156a920-29a1-553f-9c4c-fa2047002925')
