   $q$The prefix in- can mean "not," and the Latin root vis means "see." What does it mean that the cuttlefish becomes "nearly invisible"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hides itself under the sandy floor","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It becomes very easy for others to spot","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-prefix"},{"text":"It becomes very hard for others to see","is_correct":true},{"text":"It swims away much faster than others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It becomes very hard for others to see$q$, $q$In- (not) plus vis (see) plus -ible (able to be) means "not able to be seen," and the cuttlefish matches the rocks so a fish cannot spot it. Easy to spot ignores the prefix in-, which reverses the meaning.$q$, 'draft', '71faa34b-bb27-563d-a6f9-253341a2d3a5')
