   $q$The Greek root derm means "skin." Based on the root and the passage, what is the "dermis"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A thin and clear outer covering over the scales","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-details"},{"text":"A sandy patch of sea floor where it hides","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A thick layer of skin holding nerves and muscles","is_correct":true},{"text":"A muscle that pulls the color sacs wide open","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A thick layer of skin holding nerves and muscles$q$, $q$Derm means "skin," and the passage says the dermis is "a thicker layer that holds nerves, muscles and thousands of tiny color cells." The thin, clear outer layer is the epidermis, not the dermis.$q$, 'draft', '71faa34b-bb27-563d-a6f9-253341a2d3a5')
