  ('8f4576b9-3b98-57ef-b514-c0ce9ec04140', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix in- can mean "into," and the Latin root spect means "look." What does it mean to "inspect the beam carefully"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To look closely at the beam to study it","is_correct":true},{"text":"To measure how warm the beam feels","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"To shine the beam into another material","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-details"},{"text":"To block the beam from passing through","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-prefix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To look closely at the beam to study it$q$, $q$In- plus spect means "look into," so to inspect is to examine closely, which is how you would notice the beam "bends once on the way in and again on the way out." Shining the beam is the earlier step, not the inspecting.$q$, 'draft', '70e536f5-ef5f-5631-8450-c7ac7df9f16a')
