   $q$What flaw appears in the sentence "Either we teach handwriting, or we accept children who cannot think for themselves"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It relies on a statistic that the author does not explain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-fallacy"},{"text":"It uses a personal story in place of research evidence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-fallacy"},{"text":"It presents only two options when many other outcomes are possible.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It agrees with the opposing side instead of answering it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It presents only two options when many other outcomes are possible.$q$, $q$The sentence is a false choice: students could learn keyboarding and still think well, so these are not the only two possibilities. It contains no statistic or personal story.$q$, 'draft', 'f414b75c-54a2-5952-b620-2f28e72e1228')
