  ('d06e0f92-44ef-5ff9-8ee7-45f0707c47ee', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-argument-evidence'), null, 'easy',
   $q$What is Szabo's central claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Competition from the railroad, not the drought, ended the canal's working life.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The drought of 1871 was the main reason the canal failed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaims"},{"text":"Grain merchants preferred canal boats because they were cheaper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The canal carried more cargo in 1857 than in any other year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-evidence-for-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Competition from the railroad, not the drought, ended the canal's working life.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says Szabo believes "competition from the railroad, not the drought," ended the canal's working life. The drought explanation is the view she argues against.$q$, 'draft', 'b116a008-5aaa-5731-ac44-593527db3f0b')
