   $q$How does the fourth paragraph ("I understand why people like bright lights...") help advance the author's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It changes the subject from the night sky to energy bills, which is her real main point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It admits that her argument is weak, which shows she is unsure the council should act.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"It argues that sidewalk safety does not matter, which supports her case for darker streets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It concedes the safety concern and then answers it, which makes her request seem reasonable.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It concedes the safety concern and then answers it, which makes her request seem reasonable.$q$, $q$She grants that bright lights feel safe, then explains that shielded fixtures still light the ground "where people actually walk." This is a concession followed by a response, not an admission of weakness.$q$, 'draft', 'ebc360fc-3e45-5a02-8f90-48b2cd3cddcd')
