   $q$How does the repetition of "Consider" in the third paragraph advance the author's purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It lists the repairs the museum plans to make, in the order the conservators will complete them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It guides readers through the flaws one at a time and recasts each one as a clue about the quilt's past.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the author is frustrated with visitors who keep asking the same question every week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It asks readers to decide for themselves whether the flaws should be fixed, since the author is undecided.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It guides readers through the flaws one at a time and recasts each one as a clue about the quilt's past.$q$, $q$Each "Consider" sentence points to one flaw (the corner, the stain, the faded reds) and explains what it reveals about the quilt's owners. The author has clearly decided, so the paragraph is not an invitation to choose.$q$, 'draft', '6c81c09c-9abe-5798-b04e-1be1002118ed')
