   $q$Which statement best expresses the author's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Old weather records are too unreliable to be useful to scientists today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Schoolteachers in the 1880s were the hardest working people in the region.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Volunteer weather observers made essential contributions that histories have overlooked.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Inventors and professors deserve no credit for the growth of weather science.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Volunteer weather observers made essential contributions that histories have overlooked.$q$, $q$The author argues that the volunteers' records are irreplaceable and that their absence from textbooks is "a gap worth closing." He says "Those people matter" about inventors, so he does not deny them credit.$q$, 'draft', '3afc60df-1469-543f-8804-643b3b3788c0')
