   $q$How does the repeated pattern "For a teenager... For an eighty-year-old woman... For a parent..." support the author's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It lists the only groups of residents who are allowed to use benches on city streets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows a missing bench affecting different people, with the stakes rising beyond simple inconvenience.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It describes the people who complained to the author during her years at public meetings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It suggests that teenagers are the people who need benches most in the neighborhood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows a missing bench affecting different people, with the stakes rising beyond simple inconvenience.$q$, $q$The teenager faces only "an inconvenience," but for the older woman and the parent a bench "can decide whether" they go out at all, so the stakes grow with each example. The teenager is the least affected, not the most.$q$, 'draft', '2fc06731-7ede-5214-b1b1-e08f9aa49554')
