   $q$What is the author's main purpose in this essay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To change readers' negative view of vultures by showing the valuable role they play","is_correct":true},{"text":"To persuade the nature center to start a program for breeding vultures in captivity","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To explain how vultures are drawn in cartoons and why the drawings are inaccurate","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To warn readers that vultures carry diseases that can spread to pets and livestock","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To change readers' negative view of vultures by showing the valuable role they play$q$, $q$She states her goal directly: "the vulture is one of the most useful animals in our region, and one of the least appreciated." The essay says vultures destroy germs, so the claim that they spread disease reverses her point.$q$, 'draft', '99e804a9-6100-51fa-b6d6-fb4fef3eb4f3')
