   $q$What effect does the changed outcome in Text 2 have on the theme it borrows from Text 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It removes the theme of teaching others, since Ines never has to show anyone how to do a task.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It keeps the value placed on patience and teaching but softens the harsh judgment, letting hasty interns stay and grow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It makes the judgment harsher, since the interns who made mistakes lose their places in the lab.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It rejects the folktale's value on patience by showing that speed is what a modern lab truly needs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It keeps the value placed on patience and teaching but softens the harsh judgment, letting hasty interns stay and grow.$q$, $q$Dr. Osei's final words repeat Sefa's values ("finds the real cause" and "leaves the next person able"), yet no intern is sent away. He says "Anyone can learn to be fast," so the story does not favor speed.$q$, 'draft', '90729897-be3b-5689-bf8d-81e5948386b6')
