   $q$How does the ending of Text 2 revise the lesson of Text 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 warns that breaking free leads to a fall, while Text 2 suggests one can go free and stay connected in a new form.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Text 2 argues that connection is a burden, so the club is happiest once the balloon is gone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Text 2 repeats Text 1's lesson exactly, showing that anything without a string will fall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-transformation"},{"text":"Text 1 praises breaking free, while Text 2 warns that anything released will be lost for good.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 warns that breaking free leads to a fall, while Text 2 suggests one can go free and stay connected in a new form.$q$, $q$The kite learns too late that the string "held it up," but Yusra decides freedom and connection need only "the right kind of string." The balloon flies free and is still found, so Text 2 does not simply repeat the fable's warning.$q$, 'draft', '59b3cd2c-92ca-524f-9823-2f13b7c6d076')
